# deploy/ and ui/ are excluded wholesale, then the few files the image
# genuinely needs are added back.
#
# This bit CI on 2026-09-23: the dashboard was merged into this image
# (one container instead of two) and the Dockerfile started copying
# ui/server.py, ui/static/ and deploy/entrypoint.sh - all three of
# which these rules were silently hiding from the build context, so
# `docker build` failed on the COPY lines. Whenever the Dockerfile
# learns to copy something new from either directory, it needs a
# matching negation here.
deploy
!deploy/entrypoint.sh
ui
!ui/server.py
!ui/static
!ui/static/**
